#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This document describes the overall system structure of BomLens and explains "
"which tool runs at which step of the scan pipeline, and in what order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For the per-input tool flow — source code (with the ScanCode and SCANOSS "
"options), firmware, a received SBOM, and an AI model — see [Pipeline by "
"input type](pipeline-by-input.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:12
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> This document reflects the 2-stage architecture as currently "
"implemented. The Stage 1 routing in the source code (detect the language, "
"then run the official cdxgen language image) is implemented and working in "
"`scripts/scan-sbom.sh`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:13 docs/guides/by-input.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "At a glance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens is a 2-stage pipeline in which two kinds of Docker images work "
"together."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Stage 1 — Generation**: for source code, the official per-language cdxgen "
"images generate the SBOM (CycloneDX 1.6); for container images, binaries, "
"and directories, syft does."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Stage 2 — Post-processing**: the lightweight `bomlens` image takes the "
"SBOM and runs normalization, optional deep license detection, notice "
"generation, the security report, signing, and upload in order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![BomLens two-stage pipeline: per-language cdxgen images or syft build "
"bom.json, and the bomlens image post-processes "
"it](../images/diagrams/architecture-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The single entry point for orchestration is `scripts/scan-sbom.sh` "
"(`scan-sbom.bat` on Windows); this is the only script users invoke."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Why two stages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Previously, every language runtime plus every analysis tool lived in a "
"single huge image. The redesigned pipeline splits the responsibilities in "
"two."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Stage 1 image | Stage 2 image (`bomlens`) |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| **Role** | **Generates** the SBOM from source | SBOM **post-processing** "
"(normalization, notice, security, signing, upload) plus syft scans |\n"
"| **Contents** | Official **per-language** cdxgen images (java, python, "
"node, ...) | **No** language toolchain — lightweight `debian:12-slim` |\n"
"| **Acquisition** | Pulled **on demand** after detecting the project "
"language | Pulled once and reused |\n"
"| **Benefit** | cdxgen maintains up-to-date per-language toolchains | Small "
"image; pinned tool versions ensure reproducibility |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> For the five mainstream languages (java, python, node, dotnet, php), "
"detection with the official cdxgen images is identical, and for go, ruby, "
"and rust the toolchain preparation (`build-prep.sh`) is markedly better. For "
"the measurement data, see [README \"Why a Docker "
"image?\"](https://github.com/sktelecom/bomlens#why-a-docker-image-vs-plain-cdxgen).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tool inventory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The tools invoked by the pipeline and their **version pinning** status "
"(supply chain hygiene)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool | Version | Stage | Role | Enabled when |\n"
"|------|------|------|------|-----------|\n"
"| **cdxgen** | bundled in the language image | Stage 1 | Generates the SBOM "
"from source code (`--spec-version 1.6`) | `MODE=SOURCE` |\n"
"| **build-prep.sh** | — | Stage 1 | Dependency preparation right before "
"cdxgen (cargo, go, bundle, mvn, pip) | `MODE=SOURCE` |\n"
"| **syft** | `v1.51.0` | Stage 1 | Scans images, binaries, and root "
"filesystems | `MODE=IMAGE/BINARY/ROOTFS` |\n"
"| **jq** (`normalize-sbom.sh`) | — | Stage 2 | Normalizes and sorts the SBOM "
"| Always |\n"
"| **ScanCode Toolkit** | `32.5.0` | Stage 2 | Precise license detection on "
"first-party source | `--deep-license` (opt-in build) |\n"
"| **SCANOSS** | `1.54.2` | Stage 2 | Identify vendored open source in C/C++ "
"source with no package manager | `--identify-vendored` |\n"
"| **jq** (`generate-notice.sh`) | — | Stage 2 | Generates the open source "
"notice (NOTICE) | `--notice` / `--all` |\n"
"| **Trivy** | `v0.74.0` | Stage 2 | Vulnerability (CVE) security report | "
"`--security` / `--all` |\n"
"| **Cosign** | `v2.6.5` | Stage 2 | Detached SBOM signature | `--sign` |\n"
"| **curl** | — | Stage 2 | Upload to Dependency-Track | Default (unless "
"`--generate-only`) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Versions are pinned as `ARG`s in `docker/Dockerfile`. To keep the image "
"lean, ScanCode is an **opt-in** build arg (`--build-arg "
"SBOM_DEEP_LICENSE=true`). The SCANOSS client is included by default; build "
"with `--build-arg SBOM_SCANOSS=false` to drop it. Firmware "
"unpacking/identification (unblob, cve-bin-tool) ships in the separate opt-in "
"`bomlens-firmware` image, and AI-model SBOM generation (OWASP AIBOM "
"Generator) in `bomlens-aibom`. For the per-input tool flow, see [Pipeline by "
"input type](pipeline-by-input.md).\n"
msgstr ""

