#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Stage 1 — SBOM generation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid "The generation tool depends on the target type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:103
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Source code (`MODE=SOURCE`) — cdxgen language image"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`scan-sbom.sh` detects the project language with `detect_lang()`, picks the "
"matching **official cdxgen language image** with `img_for_lang()`, pulls it, "
"and runs `build-prep.sh` inside that image "
"(`scripts/scan-sbom.sh:138-208`). The lightweight post-processing image has "
"no language toolchain, so generation is handled entirely by the language "
"image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The per-language cdxgen image mapping is as follows (`scan-sbom.sh:158-177`; "
"the tag is pinned via `CDXGEN_TAG`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:121
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Detected language | Image |\n"
"|-----------|--------|\n"
"| rust | `cdxgen-debian-rust` |\n"
"| go | `cdxgen-debian-golang124` |\n"
"| ruby | `cdxgen-debian-ruby34` |\n"
"| java | `cdxgen-temurin-java21` |\n"
"| python | `cdxgen-python312` |\n"
"| node | `cdxgen-node20` |\n"
"| php | `cdxgen-debian-php84` |\n"
"| dotnet | `cdxgen-debian-dotnet9` |\n"
"| android | self-built `bomlens-android-sdk<API>` (compileSdk extracted "
"automatically) |\n"
"| mixed / unknown | cdxgen all-in-one (`CDXGEN_ALLINONE`) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid "Two steps run inside the image:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:125
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**`build-prep.sh`** (`docker/lib/build-prep.sh`) — dependency preparation "
"**right before** cdxgen. It creates lockfiles for ecosystems cdxgen cannot "
"resolve on its own (notably Rust and Go), exposing transitive "
"dependencies. POSIX `sh`, best-effort (it never fails the scan)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:133
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   | Ecosystem | Action | Notes |\n"
"   |--------|------|------|\n"
"   | Rust | `cargo generate-lockfile` | cdxgen does not run cargo "
"automatically — **required** |\n"
"   | Go | `go mod download` (`-mod=mod`) | Resolves the module graph |\n"
"   | Ruby | `bundle lock` / `install` | Only when no lockfile exists |\n"
"   | Maven | `mvn dependency:resolve` | Lightweight safety net |\n"
"   | Python | `pip install -r requirements.txt` | Exposes transitive "
"dependencies when no lockfile exists |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Run cdxgen** — `build-prep.sh` auto-detects the cdxgen binary path, which "
"differs per image, and runs `cdxgen -r --spec-version 1.6 -o bom.json` "
"(`build-prep.sh:60-73`). The generated SBOM is then handed to the Stage 2 "
"(`MODE=POSTPROCESS`) post-processing image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:136
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Image / binary / directory — syft"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:139
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**syft**, included in the `bomlens` image, generates the SBOM "
"directly. (`docker/entrypoint.sh`)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:145
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| MODE | Input | syft invocation |\n"
"|------|------|-----------|\n"
"| `IMAGE` | Docker image | `syft <image> -o cyclonedx-json` (requires the "
"docker.sock mount) |\n"
"| `BINARY` | Single file | `syft file:<path> -o cyclonedx-json` (falls back "
"to a minimal SBOM on failure) |\n"
"| `ROOTFS` | Directory | `syft dir:<path> -o cyclonedx-json` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:148
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Stage 2 — post-processing pipeline"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The `bomlens` image's entry point `run-scan` (`docker/entrypoint.sh`) takes "
"the SBOM and runs the steps in a **fixed order**. Each step is enabled by an "
"environment variable (equivalent to a CLI flag), and outputs accumulate in "
"the `ARTIFACTS` list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:153
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Stage 2 post-processing: eight fixed steps from normalize to upload, each "
"gated by its environment "
"variable](../images/diagrams/architecture-stage2-steps.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:155
#, markdown-text
msgid "Step details:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:166
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| # | Step | Script / tool | Condition | Output |\n"
"|---|------|-----------------|------|--------|\n"
"| ① | **Normalize** | `normalize-sbom.sh` (jq) | Always (deterministic mode "
"with `--byte-stable`) | Updates `bom.json` |\n"
"| ② | **Deep license** | `scancode` | `--deep-license` and `/src` exists | "
"`_scancode.json` |\n"
"| ③ | **Notice** | `generate-notice.sh` (jq) | `--notice` / `--all` | "
"`_NOTICE.txt`, `_NOTICE.html` |\n"
"| ④ | **Security report** | `scan-security.sh` (Trivy) | `--security` / "
"`--all` | `_security.{json,md,html}` |\n"
"| ⑤ | **Signing** | `cosign sign-blob` | `--sign` and `COSIGN_KEY` | "
"`bom.json.sig` |\n"
"| ⑥ | **Risk report** | `generate-risk-report.sh` | Default (skip with "
"`--no-report`) | `_risk-report.{md,html}` (plus `_conformance.*` in ANALYZE "
"mode) |\n"
"| ⑦ | **Copy to host** | `cp` | Always | Copied to `HOST_OUTPUT_DIR` |\n"
"| ⑧ | **Upload** | `curl` | Default (skipped with `--generate-only`) | "
"Upload to a Dependency-Track server or TRUSCA's native ingest (select with "
"`UPLOAD_TARGET`) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:168
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Why the order is fixed**: normalization stabilizes the input for every "
"later step, so it runs first; signing must target the final `bom.json`, so "
"it runs last. Each step is best-effort — failures are handled with `|| true` "
"or a warning and do not abort the whole scan (signing and upload "
"excepted).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:171
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Branching by input type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:174
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`scan-sbom.sh` determines the mode automatically from "
"`--git`/`--analyze`/`--firmware` and the `--target` value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:176
#, markdown-text
msgid "The checks run top to bottom; the first matching branch wins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart TD\n"
"    D1{\"--git URL<br/>or URL-like target?\"} -->|yes| R1[\"clone → "
"MODE=SOURCE\"]\n"
"    D1 -->|no| D2{\"--target<br/>*.zip / *.tar.gz?\"}\n"
"    D2 -->|yes| R2[\"extract → MODE=SOURCE\"]\n"
"    D2 -->|no| D3{\"--analyze sbom?\"}\n"
"    D3 -->|yes| R3[\"MODE=ANALYZE<br/>validate + convert to CDX\"]\n"
"    D3 -->|no| D4{\"target omitted?\"}\n"
"    D4 -->|yes| R4[\"MODE=SOURCE<br/>current directory → cdxgen\"]\n"
"    D4 -->|no| D5{\"existing file?\"}\n"
"    D5 -->|\"yes · --firmware/extension\"| R5[\"MODE=FIRMWARE<br/>opt-in "
"firmware image\"]\n"
"    D5 -->|\"yes · otherwise\"| R6[\"MODE=BINARY → syft\"]\n"
"    D5 -->|no| D6{\"existing directory?\"}\n"
"    D6 -->|yes| R7[\"MODE=ROOTFS → syft\"]\n"
"    D6 -->|no| R8[\"MODE=IMAGE → syft\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:195
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Independently of the branching above, `--ui` starts `MODE=UI` (the web "
"server `server.py`) and runs subsequent scans through the form or file "
"upload.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:207
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mode | Trigger | Generation tool | Notes |\n"
"|------|--------|-----------|------|\n"
"| `SOURCE` | No target, `--git <url>`, or `--target *.zip/*.tar.gz` | cdxgen "
"| Language detection selects the per-language image. Git targets are cloned; "
"archives are extracted and treated as source. (The web UI's SOURCE uses "
"`syft dir:` inside the container) |\n"
"| `ANALYZE` | `--analyze <sbom>` (alias `--sbom`) | — | Validates a supplier "
"SBOM (CycloneDX/SPDX), converts it to CDX, and re-aggregates. Produces "
"`_conformance.*` |\n"
"| `FIRMWARE` | `--target <file> --firmware`, or a firmware file extension | "
"unblob + syft + cve-bin-tool | **Opt-in image** `bomlens-firmware`. Details "
"in the [firmware analysis guide](../guides/firmware.md) |\n"
"| `BINARY` | `--target <file>` | syft | `file:` scheme |\n"
"| `ROOTFS` | `--target <directory>` | syft | `dir:` scheme |\n"
"| `IMAGE` | `--target <image name>` | syft | docker.sock mount |\n"
"| `AIBOM` | `--model <owner/name>` | OWASP AIBOM Generator | **Opt-in "
"image** `bomlens-aibom`. CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM from a HuggingFace model card; "
"adds a G7 conformance check |\n"
"| `MODELFILE` | `--model-file <path>` | `identify-model-file.py` (stdlib) | "
"Base image, offline. CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM read from a model file's own "
"header (GGUF, safetensors, PyTorch, pickle, npz, npy, ONNX); adds the same "
"G7 check |\n"
"| `UI` | `--ui` | — | Browser UI; runs every scan target type through the "
"form or file upload |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:210
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Flag-to-step mapping"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:213
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"How CLI flags translate into environment variables and which steps they "
"enable (`scan-sbom.sh` converts them and passes them to `entrypoint.sh`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:231
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Flag | Environment variable | Steps enabled |\n"
"|--------|----------|-------------|\n"
"| (default) | `GENERATE_REPORT=true` (plus notice and security) | normalize "
"+ **risk report** + upload |\n"
"| `--no-report` | `GENERATE_REPORT=false` | Does not force-enable the risk "
"report, notice, or security steps |\n"
"| `--notice` | `GENERATE_NOTICE=true` | ③ notice |\n"
"| `--security` | `GENERATE_SECURITY=true` | ④ security report |\n"
"| `--all` | Both of the above | ③ + ④ |\n"
"| `--git <url>` / `--branch` | (cloned on the host) | SOURCE input "
"collection |\n"
"| `--analyze <sbom>` | `MODE=ANALYZE` | Supplier SBOM validation, "
"conversion, and report |\n"
"| `--firmware` | `MODE=FIRMWARE` (firmware image) | Unpack, then syft + "
"cve-bin-tool |\n"
"| `--model <owner/name>` | `MODE=AIBOM` (aibom image) | Generate an ML-BOM "
"from a HuggingFace model, plus a G7 check |\n"
"| `--model-file <path>` | `MODE=MODELFILE` | Read one model file's header "
"into an ML-BOM, offline, plus a G7 check |\n"
"| `--deep-license` | `DEEP_LICENSE=true` | ② scancode |\n"
"| `--byte-stable` | `BYTE_STABLE=true` | ① deterministic normalization (also "
"the UI's Reproducible output toggle) |\n"
"| `--sign` | `SIGN_SBOM=true` (plus `COSIGN_KEY`/`COSIGN_PASSWORD`) | ⑤ "
"signing |\n"
"| `--generate-only` | `UPLOAD_ENABLED=false` | ⑦ skips the upload |\n"
"| `--ui` | `MODE=UI` | Web UI |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:233
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The **risk report** (`_risk-report.{md,html}`) is generated **by default** "
"in every mode (it aggregates licenses and vulnerabilities). To support it, "
"the notice and security scans are turned on automatically alongside it; "
"disable with `--no-report`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:235
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For how to use each feature, see the [notice and security report "
"guide](../guides/reports.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:238
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Artifacts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:241
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`{P}` is the project name, `{V}` the version (special characters are "
"normalized to `_`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:251
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| File | Generated when |\n"
"|------|-----------|\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json` | Always (CycloneDX 1.6; a 1.7 ML-BOM for "
"AI models) |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_NOTICE.txt` / `.html` / `.pdf` | `--notice` / `--all` "
"/ default risk report generation (PDF only in an `SBOM_PDF` build) |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_security.json` / `.md` / `.html` | `--security` / "
"`--all` / default risk report generation |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_risk-report.md` / `.html` | Default (all modes) — "
"skip with `--no-report` |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_conformance.json` / `.md` / `.html` | `--analyze` "
"(supplier SBOM validation) |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_scancode.json` | `--deep-license` |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json.sig` | `--sign` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:254
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Extension points"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:256
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding support for a new language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:260
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Check whether an official cdxgen image exists for the language — if so, add "
"it to the routing table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:260
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If cdxgen cannot resolve transitive dependencies automatically, add "
"preparation logic to `docker/lib/build-prep.sh`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:260
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Add an example project under `examples/{language}/` and a test case in "
"`tests/cases/test-{language}.sh`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:262
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For the full procedure, see the [package manager "
"guide](../contribute/package-managers.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:263
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding a new post-processing step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:265
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Add a helper script under `docker/lib/`, call it from the shared pipeline "
"section of `entrypoint.sh` (after normalization) behind an environment "
"variable guard, and append its outputs to `ARTIFACTS`. Place it **before** "
"the signing step so its outputs are covered by the signature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:268
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Design principles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Isolation** — all analysis runs in Docker containers; the host environment "
"stays untouched."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Separation of concerns** — generation (Stage 1) and post-processing (Stage "
"2) are split, keeping the post-processing image small."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Reproducibility** — tool versions are pinned via `ARG`; `--byte-stable` "
"produces byte-identical output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Standards compliance** — conforms to the CycloneDX 1.6 specification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Robustness** — post-processing steps are best-effort and do not abort the "
"whole scan."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Single interface** — every language and mode is invoked through the one "
"`scan-sbom.sh`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:279
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Division of roles (TRUSCA)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:282
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens specializes in **generation**. **Governance** — company-wide project "
"management, vulnerability triage, and license policy gates — is delegated to "
"the sister project [TRUSCA](https://github.com/trustedoss/trusca) (formerly "
"TrustedOSS Portal). Both tools share cdxgen and Trivy, so the artifacts "
"(CycloneDX) are directly compatible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (mermaid)
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:283
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flowchart TB\n"
"    subgraph dev[\"Developer · single project\"]\n"
"        direction LR\n"
"        A[\"Source / image / binary\"] --> B[\"BomLens\"]\n"
"        B --> C[\"SBOM\"]\n"
"        B --> D[\"Notice\"]\n"
"        B --> E[\"Security report\"]\n"
"    end\n"
"    subgraph org[\"Organization · central management\"]\n"
"        direction LR\n"
"        F[\"TRUSCA\"] --> G[\"Vulnerability triage\"]\n"
"        F --> H[\"License policy gate\"]\n"
"        F --> I[\"Project dashboard\"]\n"
"    end\n"
"    C -. upload .-> F\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/architecture.md:303
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Related**: [Pipeline by input type](pipeline-by-input.md) | [Getting "
"started](../start/first-scan.md) | [CLI reference](../reference/cli.md) | "
"[Use the Docker image directly](../reference/docker-image.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Why BomLens runs locally by design — what stays on your machine, how it "
"works offline, and where governance is handled instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Local-first by design"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing leaves your machine"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens runs locally, with no SaaS backend. What you analyze — source code, "
"firmware, or an SBOM someone handed you — is never sent to an external "
"service. The scan happens inside a local Docker container and ends "
"there. The outputs are written only to the directory you ran it from."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Works in closed and offline networks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens runs on air-gapped and offline networks. The few features that need "
"an external lookup can be turned off, and everything else is still "
"produced. The security report's EPSS and CISA KEV enrichment is the main "
"case: set `SECURITY_ENRICH=false` to skip it and still generate the rest of "
"the report. License lookups can likewise be skipped with "
"`FETCH_LICENSE=false`. Going the other way, three checks that sound like "
"they need the network do not: end-of-life flagging, the malicious-package "
"check and the outbound-license conflict check all read data baked into the "
"image at build time, so they keep working with no connection at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Standard, portable outputs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The outputs use standard formats — the SBOM is CycloneDX 1.6. They are not "
"tied to any single vendor, so you can verify and reuse them anywhere. When "
"you need a byte-for-byte identical SBOM for the same input, use "
"`--byte-stable`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "One scanner behind every entry point"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The three entry points — the CLI, the web UI, and the desktop app — all use "
"the same local scanner container. Only the way you drive the tool differs; "
"the behavior and the outputs are the same."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "BomLens generates; TRUSCA governs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens focuses on generation. Governance — organization-wide project "
"management, vulnerability triage, license policy gates — is delegated to the "
"sister project TRUSCA (formerly TrustedOSS Portal, "
"<https://github.com/trustedoss/trusca>). The two tools exchange CycloneDX "
"outputs directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:27 docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Related"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/local-first.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For how the two-stage pipeline works, see [How BomLens "
"works](architecture.md). For the kinds of outputs, see the [artifacts "
"reference](../reference/artifacts.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How BomLens processes each input type — source code (with ScanCode and "
"SCANOSS options), firmware, a received SBOM, and an AI model — showing which "
"open-source tool runs at each step, with diagrams."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pipeline by input type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens accepts several kinds of input — source code, firmware, an SBOM you "
"received, and an AI model. Each has its own **generation** step that builds "
"a CycloneDX SBOM, and then they all converge on one shared "
"**post-processing** pipeline (notice, security, risk report). This page "
"walks the tool flow for each input. For the high-level two-stage view, see "
"[Architecture](architecture.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Four input types converge on per-input generation and one shared "
"post-processing pipeline](../images/diagrams/pipeline-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Every external tool below is open source; the table in [Open-source tools "
"used](#open-source-tools-used) lists each one's role, license, and project "
"link."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Source code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A source folder, a GitHub URL, or a ZIP archive. Language detection picks "
"the matching official [cdxgen](https://github.com/CycloneDX/cdxgen) language "
"image, which prepares dependencies (`build-prep.sh`) and generates the "
"SBOM. When BomLens cannot run a sibling container (for example the web UI's "
"source scan), it falls back to [syft](https://github.com/anchore/syft) over "
"the directory, which captures direct dependencies from lock files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Two options apply to source scans only, and both are off by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Identify vendored OSS** (`--identify-vendored`, "
"[SCANOSS](https://github.com/scanoss/scanoss.py)) — for C/C++ and other code "
"copied in without a package manager. The SCANOSS client fingerprints files "
"and queries the hosted OSSKB service, then BomLens reconciles the matches "
"against what the package-manager scan already found and merges the rest into "
"the SBOM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Deep license detection** (`--deep-license`, [ScanCode "
"Toolkit](https://github.com/aboutcode-org/scancode-toolkit)) — scans "
"first-party source for license headers. It runs during post-processing and "
"writes a separate `_scancode.json`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Source scan flow: language detection routes to a cdxgen image with a syft "
"fallback, then optional SCANOSS before shared "
"post-processing](../images/diagrams/pipeline-source.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Container images, single binaries, and directories (root filesystems) skip "
"cdxgen and are scanned directly by syft, then follow the same "
"post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Firmware"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A network-device firmware image (`.bin`, `.img.gz`, squashfs, and more), "
"handled by the opt-in `bomlens-firmware` image. Firmware packs an OS and "
"dozens of libraries into one sealed file, so BomLens first unpacks it, then "
"identifies components in two ways: package-manager metadata with syft, and "
"stripped static binaries with "
"[cve-bin-tool](https://github.com/intel/cve-bin-tool) (which also matches "
"CVEs). The two results merge, and a CPE/SPDX enrichment step fills "
"identifiers for a curated list of well-known OSS (busybox, dropbear, "
"dnsmasq, …) so Trivy and the notice can use them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Unpacking tries tools in order, using the first that succeeds: "
"[unblob](https://github.com/onekey-sec/unblob) (primary), `unsquashfs` for "
"standard squashfs, `7z` for the container formats Windows deliveries arrive "
"in, then `binwalk`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Firmware flow: unpack, find the root filesystem, scan with syft and "
"cve-bin-tool in parallel, then merge, enrich, and "
"post-process](../images/diagrams/pipeline-firmware.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The firmware tools are GPL-family, so they live only in the "
"`bomlens-firmware` image and the base image installs none of them. See the "
"[firmware guide](../guides/firmware.md) and its limits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Received SBOM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"An SBOM (CycloneDX or SPDX) received from a supplier or another team — no "
"source code needed. BomLens first checks it against the quality criteria and "
"writes a conformance report, then normalizes the input to CycloneDX so the "
"rest of the pipeline can analyze it. SPDX is converted with `syft convert` "
"(a `jq` fallback handles SPDX JSON if syft is unavailable). Notice, "
"security, and the risk report are always produced in this mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Received SBOM flow: validate for conformance, convert SPDX to CycloneDX, "
"then shared post-processing](../images/diagrams/pipeline-analyze.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Validation is based on the original input before conversion, so SPDX is "
"checked as SPDX. Details are in the [supplier SBOM "
"guide](../guides/supplier-sbom.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A Yocto build directory enters here too. Pointing `--target` at one is "
"recognized, and the image SBOM the build published under "
"`tmp/deploy/images/` takes this same path — read by a dedicated parser that "
"keeps the installed package set and the vulnerability verdicts the build "
"recorded, rather than by the generic SPDX conversion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "AI model"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A HuggingFace model id (`org/model`), handled by the opt-in `bomlens-aibom` "
"image. The [OWASP AIBOM "
"Generator](https://github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/aibom-generator) "
"fetches the model-card metadata over the network and builds a CycloneDX 1.7 "
"ML-BOM centered on the model and its datasets. Post-processing then adds a "
"G7 minimum-element conformance check. Because an AI model has no package "
"CVEs, the security report is skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![AI model flow: the OWASP AIBOM Generator builds a CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM "
"that goes through shared "
"post-processing](../images/diagrams/pipeline-ai-model.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There is a second AI input that runs entirely in the base image: a model "
"**file** (`--model-file`, or a model upload in the web UI). No generator and "
"no network are involved — a stdlib reader parses the file's own header, "
"decides the format from its magic bytes rather than its name, hashes the "
"file, and writes the same CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM shape, which then takes the "
"identical post-processing. It is the path for weights a supplier sent you "
"and for models that were never published. What it can fill depends on the "
"format: GGUF declares a name, a license and an architecture, safetensors "
"usually declares only tensor shapes, and a file that declares neither still "
"contributes its integrity hash."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The model card's disclosure (weights, architecture, training data, "
"training process) and the G7 result appear in the web UI's Models & datasets "
"and G7 sections — see the [web UI reference](../reference/ui.md). For a "
"step-by-step walkthrough, see the [AI model guide](../guides/ai-model.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shared post-processing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Whatever the input, the SBOM flows through the same ordered "
"steps. Normalization runs first to stabilize the input for every later step; "
"signing runs last so it covers the final SBOM. Dashed steps are optional or "
"input-specific. Each step is best-effort — a failure is skipped with a "
"warning rather than aborting the scan (signing and upload excepted)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Shared post-processing steps in order from normalize to artifacts, with "
"optional steps dashed](../images/diagrams/pipeline-postprocess.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The risk report is generated by default in every mode (it aggregates "
"licenses and vulnerabilities); skip it with `--no-report`. For the "
"step-by-step flag mapping, see "
"[Architecture](architecture.md#flag-to-step-mapping)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Open-source tools used"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Every analysis tool is open source. The tools installed into the base image "
"are permissively licensed; the GPL ones are isolated in the opt-in "
"`bomlens-firmware` image, and the AI generator in `bomlens-aibom`. Every "
"image also carries the GPL system packages of its Debian base, as any Linux "
"image does — see [Third-party "
"licenses](https://github.com/sktelecom/bomlens/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:94
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool | Role | Input | License | Image | Project |\n"
"|------|------|-------|---------|-------|---------|\n"
"| cdxgen | Generate the SBOM from source | source | Apache-2.0 | language "
"images | [CycloneDX/cdxgen](https://github.com/CycloneDX/cdxgen) |\n"
"| syft | SBOM for images, binaries, directories, firmware rootfs | source "
"(fallback), image, binary, rootfs, firmware | Apache-2.0 | base / firmware | "
"[anchore/syft](https://github.com/anchore/syft) |\n"
"| SCANOSS (scanoss.py) | Identify vendored OSS via file fingerprints | "
"source (`--identify-vendored`) | MIT | base | "
"[scanoss/scanoss.py](https://github.com/scanoss/scanoss.py) |\n"
"| ScanCode Toolkit | Deep first-party license detection | source "
"(`--deep-license`) | Apache-2.0 | base (opt-in) | "
"[aboutcode-org/scancode-toolkit](https://github.com/aboutcode-org/scancode-toolkit) "
"|\n"
"| unblob | Firmware unpacking (primary) | firmware | MIT | firmware | "
"[onekey-sec/unblob](https://github.com/onekey-sec/unblob) |\n"
"| sasquatch | Vendor squashfs variants standard unsquashfs refuses | "
"firmware | GPL-2.0 | firmware (opt) | "
"[onekey-sec/sasquatch](https://github.com/onekey-sec/sasquatch) |\n"
"| cve-bin-tool | Stripped-binary identification + CVE matching | firmware | "
"GPL-3.0 | firmware | "
"[intel/cve-bin-tool](https://github.com/intel/cve-bin-tool) |\n"
"| OWASP AIBOM Generator | ML-BOM from a HuggingFace model card | AI model | "
"Apache-2.0 | aibom | "
"[GenAI-Security-Project/aibom-generator](https://github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/aibom-generator) "
"|\n"
"| Trivy | Vulnerability (CVE) security report | all | Apache-2.0 | base | "
"[aquasecurity/trivy](https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy) |\n"
"| cosign | Detached SBOM signature | all (`--sign`) | Apache-2.0 | base | "
"[sigstore/cosign](https://github.com/sigstore/cosign) |\n"
"| WeasyPrint | Optional PDF rendering of the notice | all (`SBOM_PDF` build) "
"| BSD-3-Clause | base (opt-in) | "
"[Kozea/WeasyPrint](https://github.com/Kozea/WeasyPrint) |\n"
"| jq | SBOM normalization, notice, report assembly | all | MIT | base | "
"[jqlang/jq](https://github.com/jqlang/jq) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> For the full license inventory and the GPL source-offer for the firmware "
"image, see "
"[THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md](https://github.com/sktelecom/bomlens/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/pipeline-by-input.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Related**: [Architecture](architecture.md) | [Firmware "
"guide](../guides/firmware.md) | [Supplier SBOM "
"guide](../guides/supplier-sbom.md) | [Identify bundled "
"OSS](../guides/identify-vendored.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How to read and interpret the open-source notice, the security report, and "
"the open-source risk report that BomLens produces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What the reports mean"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This page explains how to read and interpret BomLens reports after a "
"scan. For how to produce them, see [Generating "
"reports](../guides/reports.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What the notice handles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The open-source notice (NOTICE) groups components by license. Beyond that "
"grouping, it also handles the following."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It normalizes license names to SPDX identifiers. For example, \"Apache "
"License, version 2.0\" is normalized to `Apache-2.0`. Entries that were "
"duplicated because the same license was written differently are merged into "
"one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When the scan tool could not name a license and left it as `CUSTOM` with the "
"license file text attached (common for Go modules whose LICENSE file "
"rewrites the copyright lines), the text itself is checked against the "
"wording of major licenses (`MIT`, `BSD-2-Clause`, `BSD-3-Clause`, "
"`Apache-2.0`, `ISC`) and the SPDX identifier is recovered. A text that stays "
"ambiguous is kept as `CUSTOM` rather than guessed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the SBOM has a copyright value, it is shown per component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The full SPDX standard texts of 21 major open-source licenses (`Apache-2.0`, "
"`MIT`, `BSD-3-Clause`, the `GPL`/`LGPL` families, and so on) are bundled at "
"the end of the notice. This satisfies the obligation of licenses that "
"require the full text, without separate collection. The bundled originals "
"are in `docker/lib/licenses/*.txt`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Priority signals (CVSS, EPSS, CISA KEV)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Severity alone makes it hard to decide what to fix first. To help with that, "
"the security report shows three more signals beyond severity. The Markdown "
"and HTML table columns are `Severity | KEV | CVSS | EPSS | CVE | Package | "
"Installed | Fixed`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**CVSS** — the technical severity score of the vulnerability (0–10). The V3 "
"score is used first, falling back to V2 if absent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**EPSS** — the probability of real-world exploitation within the next 30 "
"days (0–1). Queried from FIRST.org; a higher score means a greater chance of "
"being used in an attack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**CISA KEV** — whether it is on the \"known exploited vulnerabilities\" list "
"maintained by the US CISA. If it is, the HTML report marks it with a ⚠️ "
"badge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The table puts KEV-listed items at the top, then sorts by severity, and "
"finally by EPSS descending. Working top-down naturally addresses the "
"highest-risk items first. This is specific to the static report file; the "
"[web UI's vulnerabilities table](../reference/ui.md#result-sections) opens "
"sorted by severity then CVSS instead, and lets you re-sort by any column, "
"including EPSS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"EPSS and KEV require external API lookups. On an air-gapped network, set "
"`SECURITY_ENRICH=false` to omit the two columns and still generate the rest "
"of the report."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Outbound-license conflicts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The license classification above labels each component's copyleft strength "
"on its own. Whether that strength is actually a problem depends on the "
"license *you* distribute under, which a source scan cannot infer — so you "
"declare it with `--license <spdx-id>` (or the web UI's Outbound license "
"field), and each dependency is then judged against it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`Cannot be met` — the dependency's terms cannot be satisfied while shipping "
"under your declared license."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`Depends on how you ship` — permitted, but the obligations turn on how you "
"link or distribute. A person has to look."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`Cannot judge` — the license was not recognised, or you declared none."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A license carrying an exception clause (the classpath exception being the "
"common one) never lands in the first bucket: that clause exists precisely to "
"permit the combination."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Declare nothing and the check does not run — the report simply omits the "
"section rather than printing a clean bill nobody checked. It is a "
"documentation aid, not a legal determination: see the [CLI "
"reference](../reference/cli.md) for the flag and [Web "
"UI](../reference/ui.md) for where the verdicts appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Known-malicious packages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A vulnerability says an honest package has a flaw. A malicious package is a "
"different thing: it was published to attack whoever installs it — a "
"typosquat of a name you meant to type, a release pushed from a hijacked "
"maintainer account, a payload that runs during installation. BomLens flags "
"these separately from the vulnerability table, because the response is "
"different. You remove the package, and you rotate any credential the build "
"could reach; there is no version to upgrade to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Matching is by PURL, never by name. These packages are deliberately named to "
"resemble real ones, so a name match is exactly the wrong tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The data is a bundled snapshot of the malicious-package advisories OSV "
"publishes (the ones carrying a `MAL-` id), so the check runs offline like "
"the EOL flag. Set `ENRICH_MALICIOUS=false` to skip it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Most advisories name no versions, which means every published version of "
"that package is malicious. When an advisory does name versions, only those "
"are flagged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Each flagged component carries the advisory id and the snapshot date "
"(`bomlens:malicious:id`, `bomlens:malicious:source`). The date matters: this "
"is a fast-moving area, so a clean result means \"not in this snapshot\", not "
"\"safe today\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Component end-of-life (EOL)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens also flags whether each component's release cycle has reached its "
"upstream end-of-life. This is a supply-chain risk separate from CVEs: a "
"runtime or framework past its support date gets no more upstream security "
"fixes, so a Critical or High reported later has no patch to apply."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The dates come from a snapshot of endoflife.date bundled into the scanner "
"image, so the check runs offline with no network call and works "
"air-gapped. The source and snapshot date are recorded on each flagged "
"component (`bomlens:eol:source`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Coverage follows endoflife.date, which tracks runtimes, major frameworks, "
"operating systems and databases (spring-boot, express, django, nodejs, "
"python, php, nginx, openssl, ubuntu, debian, and so on). Most smaller "
"libraries are not tracked, and a component with no mapping is left unknown "
"rather than guessed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the web UI, the Overview shows an \"End of life\" count tile, with the "
"components that are also vulnerable highlighted in the risk colour — an EOL "
"component gets no upstream patch for its CVEs, so that is the set to act "
"on. The Components table adds an \"End of life\" badge, with the EOL date "
"where known, and an \"End of life\" filter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is on by default and adds no delay because it is offline. To turn it off, "
"set `ENRICH_EOL=false`. AI/ML model scans skip it, since they have no "
"runtime or framework components."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:60
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Version currency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Sitting on a supported release cycle is not the same as running its latest "
"version, so BomLens also flags whether a component has fallen behind. This "
"works in two layers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The offline layer is on by default, alongside the EOL check. The same "
"endoflife.date snapshot records the latest patch of each release cycle, so "
"BomLens can tell offline whether the installed version trails the newest "
"patch within its own cycle. That is a safe, in-cycle upgrade found with no "
"network call, exactly like the EOL check. A component that is behind carries "
"`bomlens:currency:outdated=true`, with the target patch in "
"`bomlens:currency:latestPatch`. It runs inside the EOL step, so "
"`ENRICH_EOL=false` turns it off as well, and AI/ML model scans skip it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The deps.dev layer is opt-in. Set `STALENESS_ENRICH=true` to look each "
"component up on deps.dev, Google's public package metadata, and record the "
"absolute newest version (`bomlens:staleness:latest`), how many releases the "
"installed one is behind (`bomlens:staleness:releasesBehind`), and when the "
"newest version shipped (`bomlens:staleness:lastReleased`). This makes one "
"network call per component, so it trades the scan's offline determinism for "
"freshness. It does not suit an air-gapped run, which is why it is off by "
"default. It is best-effort and time-bounded, so a failed lookup never aborts "
"the scan. The supported ecosystems are npm, PyPI, Maven, Go, Cargo, NuGet "
"and RubyGems. Whether a project is still actively maintained is not part of "
"this release; it is planned for a later release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the web UI, the Overview adds a count tile for components behind their "
"latest version, and the Components table marks a component that is not on "
"its latest version and adds an \"Outdated\" filter. With the deps.dev layer "
"on, each such component also shows how many releases it is behind and its "
"last-release date."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Interpreting results & follow-up"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Severity | Meaning | Recommended action |\n"
"|----------|---------|--------------------|\n"
"| **Critical** | immediately exploitable, severe | upgrade to the `Fixed` "
"version as the top priority |\n"
"| **High** | high risk | plan a patch in the short term |\n"
"| **Medium / Low** | limited impact | handle during regular maintenance |\n"
"| **Unknown** | severity not assessed | check the CVE directly and classify "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the report's `Fixed` column has a version, raising the dependency to that "
"version or higher resolves it. This is the fastest first response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid "CI gate example. Fail the build if there is even one Critical:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  crit=$(jq '[.Results[]?.Vulnerabilities[]? | "
"select(.Severity==\"CRITICAL\")] | length' *_security.json)\n"
"  [ \"$crit\" -gt 0 ] && { echo \"${crit} Critical vulnerabilities\"; exit "
"1; }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Triage — judging false positives (no real impact) and approving exceptions — "
"and history management are beyond the scope of BomLens. Upload the SBOM to a "
"vulnerability management system (Dependency-Track, TRUSCA, etc.) to handle "
"it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:85
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The open-source risk report"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:88
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The open-source risk report aggregates vulnerabilities by severity with "
"recommended response deadlines (Critical 7 days, High 30 days). It includes "
"a license summary, and for a supplier SBOM it adds the format conformance "
"result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The license summary also classifies components by copyleft strength, with "
"the same rules the web UI uses. Each component in the SBOM carries a "
"`bomlens:licenseClass` property holding one of `network-copyleft`, "
"`strong-copyleft`, `weak-copyleft`, `permissive` or `uncategorized`, and the "
"report shows a per-class count plus the components that drive the copyleft "
"exposure. A license the tool does not recognize is never assumed permissive; "
"it stays `uncategorized` for a human to review."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Generating reports](../guides/reports.md)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Artifacts reference](../reference/artifacts.md)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid "[How BomLens works](architecture.md)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What an SBOM (Software Bill of Materials) is, why open-source notices and "
"vulnerability response depend on one, and what CycloneDX, PURL, and ML-BOM "
"mean — a five-minute primer before your first scan."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is an SBOM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"An SBOM (Software Bill of Materials) is a list of the components inside a "
"piece of software: every open-source library and package it ships with, each "
"with its name, version, and license. It plays the same role for software "
"that a list of ingredients plays for packaged food — you can see what is "
"inside without taking the product apart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Most software today is assembled largely from open source. A typical web "
"application directly declares a few dozen packages, and those pull in "
"hundreds more. Nobody can keep that inventory in their head, so the SBOM is "
"generated from the project by a tool — that is what BomLens does."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Why you need one"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Two everyday jobs depend on knowing exactly what is inside your software."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Meeting license obligations.** Most open-source licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, "
"BSD, and others) require you to ship a copyright notice and the license text "
"along with your product. To write that open-source notice you first need the "
"component list — the SBOM. BomLens generates the notice from the SBOM in the "
"same run.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Responding to vulnerabilities.** When a vulnerability is announced in a "
"library, the first question is \"do we ship it, and in which "
"version?\". With an SBOM per product, that answer is a lookup instead of an "
"investigation. This is also why customers and regulators increasingly ask "
"suppliers to hand over an SBOM with each delivery.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Terms you will meet in the results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**CycloneDX** is the standard file format BomLens writes its SBOMs in — a "
"JSON document defined by the [OWASP CycloneDX](https://cyclonedx.org/) "
"project (version 1.6). Because the format is standard, the file you generate "
"can be read by other tools: vulnerability trackers, policy checkers, or a "
"customer's own tooling.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**PURL** (Package URL) is the identifier each component carries inside the "
"SBOM, such as `pkg:npm/express@4.18.2`. It names the ecosystem (npm, Maven, "
"PyPI, and so on), the package, and the exact version in one string, so every "
"tool that reads the SBOM agrees on which component is meant.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**ML-BOM** is the same idea applied to an AI model: a CycloneDX document "
"listing what a model is made of — its datasets, base model, and "
"license. BomLens generates one from a HuggingFace model id; see the [AI "
"model guide](../guides/ai-model.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:27 docs/guides/ai-model.md:181
#: docs/start/first-scan.md:168
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "You do not need to remember any of this to run a scan. Pick your path:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"No command line: the [no-CLI quick start](../start/no-cli.md) goes from "
"install to an open-source notice in clicks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "Developer setup, web UI and CLI: [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Related**: [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md) | [No-CLI quick "
"start](../start/no-cli.md) | [Artifacts](../reference/artifacts.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Add support for a new programming language or package manager to BomLens, "
"step by step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding a package manager"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide walks through adding support for a new programming language or "
"package manager, step by step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:9 docs/guides/ai-model.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check the following before adding a new language or package manager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**cdxgen support**: Check the [cdxgen supported project "
"types](https://github.com/CycloneDX/cdxgen#supported-project-types). If an "
"official cdxgen language image exists, adding it to the routing table is "
"enough."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**syft support**: If you need binary or image analysis, check the [syft "
"supported ecosystems](https://github.com/anchore/syft#supported-ecosystems)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Need for a custom analyzer**: Consider a custom analysis script only when "
"neither tool supports the ecosystem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Source scanning is a two-stage design that routes to per-language official "
"cdxgen images rather than using a single image. See "
"[Architecture](../concepts/architecture.md) for the full picture."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Add language detection and image routing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`docker/lib/source-detect.sh` is the shared detection logic used by both the "
"CLI and the web UI. Modify two functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`detect_lang()` — add a rule that detects the language from the project's "
"manifest files (for example, Kotlin checks for `build.gradle.kts` — Kotlin "
"is already covered by the `java` branch)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`img_for_lang()` — add the official cdxgen image that corresponds to the "
"detected language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# img_for_lang() example — add a new language entry\n"
"newlang) echo \"ghcr.io/cyclonedx/cdxgen-debian-newlang:$CDXGEN_TAG\" ;;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Update build-prep.sh if dependency preparation is needed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If cdxgen cannot resolve transitive dependencies in the ecosystem without a "
"lock file, add preparation logic to `docker/lib/build-prep.sh`, which "
"creates lock files right before cdxgen runs. Rust (`cargo "
"generate-lockfile`) and Go (`go mod download`) are existing "
"precedents. Write the preparation as best-effort so it never fails the scan."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Add an example project"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add an example project under the `examples/` directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"examples/kotlin/\n"
"├── README.md              # Example description\n"
"├── build.gradle.kts       # Build file\n"
"├── gradle.lockfile        # Lock file (required!)\n"
"└── src/main/kotlin/\n"
"    └── Main.kt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Why the lock file matters**: cdxgen extracts exact version information "
"from lock files. Without one, dependency detection is incomplete.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Add a test"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Create a `tests/cases/test-{언어}.sh` file. See the [testing "
"guide](testing.md#writing-tests) for details on how to write it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/contribute/package-managers.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n"
"set -euo pipefail\n"
"\n"
"source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../helpers/assert.sh\"\n"
"source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/../helpers/setup.sh\"\n"
"\n"
"TEST_NAME=\"Kotlin Gradle 소스 코드 분석\"\n"
"EXAMPLE_DIR=\"examples/kotlin\"\n"
"\n"
"setup_test \"$TEST_NAME\"\n"
"\n"
"run_scan \\\n"
"  --project \"KotlinExample\" \\\n"
"  --version \"1.0.0\" \\\n"
"  --target \"$EXAMPLE_DIR\" \\\n"
"  --generate-only\n"
"\n"
"assert_file_exists \"KotlinExample_1.0.0_bom.json\"\n"
"assert_json_field \".bomFormat\" \"CycloneDX\"\n"
"assert_json_field \".specVersion\" \"1.6\"\n"
