#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/testing.md:139
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function | Description |\n"
"|------|------|\n"
"| `assert_file_exists <file>` | Checks that a file exists |\n"
"| `assert_json_field <field> <expected>` | Checks a JSON field value |\n"
"| `assert_components_count_gte <count>` | Checks that the component count is "
"at least N |\n"
"| `assert_purl_prefix <prefix>` | Checks the PURL prefix format |\n"
"| `assert_license_exists` | Checks that at least one license entry exists "
"|\n"
"| `assert_no_empty_versions` | Checks that no version field is empty |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/contribute/testing.md:140
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Test writing principles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/testing.md:143
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Independence**: Each test must not depend on other tests. Results must "
"stay the same regardless of test order.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/testing.md:145
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Cleanup**: Always delete generated files in `teardown_test` so they do not "
"affect the next test.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/testing.md:147
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Clear names**: `TEST_NAME` should clearly express what the test "
"verifies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/contribute/testing.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Minimal assertions**: Assert only what is needed and avoid excessive "
"checks.\n"
msgstr ""

