"`_security.md` — a per-severity tally table and CVE list. Good to attach to "
"a PR or issue."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/reports.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid "`_security.html` — a visual report with severity badges and tables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The report does not fail the scan even when vulnerabilities exist "
"(report-only). If you need a gate, post-process `_security.json`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:116
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For severity, CVSS, EPSS, and KEV priority signals and follow-up "
"interpretation, see [What the reports "
"mean](../concepts/reports-explained.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/reports.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deep CVE matching (`--deep-cve`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Trivy matches vulnerabilities by package identity (PURL), which covers the "
"ecosystem advisory databases well. Some CVEs in older Java libraries, "
"however, are recorded only in the NVD against a CPE identifier, so a "
"PURL-based scan never reaches them. `--deep-cve` adds a second pass: BomLens "
"derives an NVD-matchable CPE for each Maven component from its groupId (that "
"enrichment step targets Maven), then grype matches every component's CPE, "
"whatever ecosystem it came from, against a bundled NVD database. In practice "
"most of the extra findings are still Maven, since that is where the "
"enrichment adds a CPE the SBOM did not already carry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/reports.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project \"MyApp\" --version \"1.0.0\" --deep-cve "
"--generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/reports.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`--deep-cve` implies `--security`. The extra findings merge into the same "
"security report (`_security.json/.md/.html`), tagged with their `nvd:cpe` "
"source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/reports.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The scan runs on the opt-in `ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-deep-cve:latest` "
"image, which bundles grype and its database; it is pulled automatically when "
"the flag is set (override with `SBOM_DEEP_CVE_IMAGE`). It applies to the "
"base-image modes (source, image, binary, rootfs, SBOM analysis); a firmware "
"or AI-model scan prints a warning and runs without grype, since neither "
"produces package purls for it to match."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/reports.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the web UI (and the desktop app), the same option is the **Deep CVE "
"matching (NVD CPE)** toggle in the scan options. It is offered on every scan "
"mode that uses the base image — source, Docker image, rootfs, package "
"upload, and SBOM upload — and hidden only for firmware and AI-model scans, "
"matching the CLI. Turning it on switches the security report on too, and the "
"deep-cve image downloads once on first use, either as a sibling container or "
"in-process if the UI itself was launched from that image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/reports.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"CPE matching is looser than PURL matching, because NVD version ranges can be "
"recorded coarsely. By default the scan stays offline: such findings are kept "
"and marked **version-unverified** in the report (a dagger with a footnote), "
"so a reader knows which rows may be loose-version false positives. To "
"tighten them, set `SECURITY_NVD_VERIFY=true` with an `NVD_API_KEY`: each "
"finding is then checked against the live NVD version range and out-of-range "
"false positives are dropped. The verification needs network access and adds "
"minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/reports.md:132
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SECURITY_NVD_VERIFY=true NVD_API_KEY=\"your-key\" \\\n"
"  ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project \"MyApp\" --version \"1.0.0\" --deep-cve "
"--generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/reports.md:139
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deep license detection (`--deep-license`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The basic notice covers the licenses of dependencies "
"(third-party). `--deep-license` uses scancode-toolkit to also detect license "
"headers in the project's own source code (first-party)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/reports.md:143
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project \"MyApp\" --version \"1.0.0\" --notice "
"--deep-license --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:148
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the web UI, deep license detection is one of the Generation "
"options. Either way it relies on scancode, which is heavy and slow (minutes "
"to tens of minutes for a large repo) and is not in the base image. To use "
"it, run from an image that bundles scancode:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:154
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> ```bash\n"
"> docker build --build-arg SBOM_DEEP_LICENSE=true -t bomlens:deep ./docker\n"
"> # CLI:    SBOM_SCANNER_IMAGE=bomlens:deep ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh "
"... --deep-license\n"
"> # Web UI: SBOM_SCANNER_IMAGE=bomlens:deep ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui\n"
"> ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:156
#, markdown-text
msgid "Additional output: `MyApp_1.0.0_scancode.json`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/reports.md:159
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Outbound-license conflicts (`--license`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:162
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Declares the license you distribute under, so each dependency can be judged "
"against it. A source scan cannot infer this — cdxgen leaves the root license "
"empty for maven and gradle trees — so without the flag no verdict is "
"produced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/reports.md:163
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project \"MyApp\" --version \"1.0.0\" --license "
"Apache-2.0 --all --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:168
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The value is recorded on the SBOM's root component, and the risk report "
"gains a conflict section. An existing root license — a supplier SBOM's own "
"declaration — is never replaced. For how to read the verdicts see [What the "
"reports mean](../concepts/reports-explained.md#outbound-license-conflicts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/reports.md:171
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic output (`--byte-stable`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:174
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Produces a byte-identical SBOM for the same input. It removes meaningless "
"diffs in CI (timestamps, random IDs, ordering differences) and ensures "
"reproducibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/reports.md:175
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project \"MyApp\" --version \"1.0.0\" --byte-stable "
"--generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:180
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"What it does: fixes `metadata.timestamp` to `1970-01-01T00:00:00Z`, removes "
"the random `serialNumber`, sorts `components` by purl, and sorts keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/reports.md:183
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SBOM signing (`--sign`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:186
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Creates a detached signature on the SBOM with cosign to establish "
"supply-chain trust. It is offline key-based signing (`--tlog-upload=false`), "
"so no network or OIDC is needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/reports.md:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# 1) Generate a key (first time only). For a passwordless key, use "
"COSIGN_PASSWORD=\"\"\n"
"docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/keys -w /keys -e COSIGN_PASSWORD=\"\" \\\n"
"  --entrypoint cosign ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest generate-key-pair\n"
"\n"
"# 2) Scan while signing (COSIGN_KEY=private key path, COSIGN_PASSWORD=key "
"password)\n"
"COSIGN_KEY=\"$PWD/cosign.key\" COSIGN_PASSWORD=\"\" \\\n"
"  ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project MyApp --version 1.0.0 --sign "
"--generate-only\n"
"\n"
"# 3) Verify\n"
"docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/w -w /w --entrypoint cosign \\\n"
"  ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest \\\n"
"  verify-blob --key cosign.pub --signature MyApp_1.0.0_bom.json.sig \\\n"
"  --insecure-ignore-tlog MyApp_1.0.0_bom.json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:204
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The private key is mounted read-only into the container. Additional output: "
"`MyApp_1.0.0_bom.json.sig`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/reports.md:207 docs/reference/cli.md:125
#: docs/reference/ecosystems.md:224
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/reports.md:215
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Symptom | Cause / fix |\n"
"|---------|-------------|\n"
"| `trivy not installed ... skipping` | old image. Pull the latest image with "
"`docker pull`. |\n"
"| `--deep-license requested but scancode not in image` | build the image "
"with `--build-arg SBOM_DEEP_LICENSE=true`. |\n"
"| `Docker is not running` in the UI | start the Docker engine (Rancher "
"Desktop/Docker Desktop, etc.) and run it again. |\n"
"| Many `NOASSERTION` in the notice | the dependencies have no license "
"metadata. Supplement with `--deep-license` or check manually. |\n"
"| Port conflict (`--ui`) | specify a different port with `UI_PORT`. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How to build an SBOM for a server — scan the OS rootfs, the application, and "
"the static-link dependencies as separate layers, merging into one BOM only "
"when an external system requires it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Server SBOM guide"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A server is not a single source tree. It is an operating system, the "
"application installed on top of it, and libraries that were linked into the "
"binaries during the build. A scan of any one of these misses the others, "
"which is the usual reason a server SBOM ends up incomplete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide treats a server as two layers — the OS and the application — and "
"scans each with BomLens. Keep the layer SBOMs separate — that is the "
"default, and it keeps each one reviewable on its own. Merge them into one "
"product SBOM only when an external system asks for a single file (see "
"[Optional: merge into one SBOM](#optional-merge-into-one-sbom))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer | What it covers | Symptom if omitted |\n"
"|-------|----------------|--------------------|\n"
"| OS | The OS and its installed packages (e.g. CentOS plus everything in the "
"rpm database) | OS vulnerabilities missing |\n"
"| Application | The target application and its package-manager dependencies, "
"direct and transitive | Application dependencies missing |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Beyond the two layers, statically linked libraries (for example an openssl "
"or liblfds built into the binary) are a blind spot. A package manager does "
"not declare them and the OS package database does not list them, so neither "
"layer's scan finds them. They have to be detected and recorded separately, "
"and missing them is the most common omission — see [Static-link "
"libraries](#static-link-libraries-a-blind-spot-of-both-layers) below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"One tool, BomLens, produces both layers; only the input changes. The "
"requirement is that the OS, the application, and the static-link libraries "
"are all accounted for — not that they end up in one file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Windows**: the commands here are for macOS/Linux. See [Getting "
"started](../start/first-scan.md) for the `scan-sbom.bat` and WSL2 "
"equivalents.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Docker 20.10+ required. Pull the scanner image once.\n"
"docker pull ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest\n"
"\n"
"# Keep the script path in a variable.\n"
"SBOM=/path/to/bomlens/scripts/scan-sbom.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 1 — OS packages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Scan the server's rootfs (the extracted root filesystem) or a container "
"image of it. Syft reads the rpm/dpkg/apk database and records every "
"installed package with a real purl (`pkg:rpm/...`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# A rootfs directory:\n"
"$SBOM --project mms-relay-os --version 6.10 \\\n"
"  --target /path/to/server-rootfs \\\n"
"  --all --generate-only\n"
"\n"
"# Or, if the server is packaged as a container image:\n"
"$SBOM --project mms-relay-os --version 6.10 \\\n"
"  --target mms-relay:6.10 \\\n"
"  --all --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The target must contain the package database. A folder holding only unpacked "
"install files, with no rpm database, yields empty purls and a useless "
"result. Use the real rootfs or image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Layer 2 — Application code and dependencies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Scan the application source after the build. With a package manager (Maven, "
"npm, pip, Go modules, Conan, and others), transitive dependencies resolve "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cd /path/to/app-source\n"
"$SBOM --project mms-relay-app --version 2.0.0 --all --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Build first. Scanning before the build or install leaves transitive "
"dependencies unresolved. For a pure CMake/Make application with no manifest, "
"the component list is sparse; add `--deep-license` to record the first-party "
"source licenses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Static-link libraries (a blind spot of both layers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Source scanners do not see libraries that were statically linked into a "
"binary, and neither does the OS package database — this is the blind spot "
"the two layers leave. There is no fully automatic path, so combine two "
"approaches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Analyze the build-output binary or firmware image to catch what tooling can "
"find:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$SBOM --project mms-relay-bin --version 2.0.0 \\\n"
"  --target /path/to/delivered-binary \\\n"
"  --all --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For what the scan still misses, record the source and version by hand from "
"the build script — for example the openssl release the build pulls in "
"(`openssl 1.1.1za`). For a more precise inventory of statically linked "
"components, you can add a binary composition analysis tool as a "
"complementary check."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:77
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Verify each layer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Keep the per-layer SBOMs (and the static-link SBOM) as they are. Check each "
"one — not a combined file — so a gap is caught where it belongs. Confirm it "
"is well formed and that its components carry real purls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:81
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for bom in mms-relay-os_6.10_bom.json mms-relay-app_2.0.0_bom.json "
"mms-relay-bin_2.0.0_bom.json; do\n"
"  echo \"$bom: $(jq '.components | length' \"$bom\") components, \\\n"
"$(jq '[.components[] | select(.purl)] | length' \"$bom\") with purl\"\n"
"done\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:89
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The two counts should be close for each layer. A large gap means many "
"components lack a purl, which usually points to a raw-directory scan or a "
"hand-written entry. Then validate the schema with the [CycloneDX "
"validator](https://github.com/CycloneDX/cyclonedx-cli)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:91
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Keeping the layers separate is the default for a reason: a reviewer sees at "
"a glance which layer is missing or where a vulnerability sits, and each "
"layer's dependency graph stays cleanly scoped to that layer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:92
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optional: merge into one SBOM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Merge only when an external system expects a single product BOM "
"(Dependency-Track and TRUSCA both register one BOM per project). `--merge` "
"combines the layers, dedupes components by purl, and stamps the top-level "
"component with the product name and version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$SBOM --project mms-relay-server --version 1.0.0 \\\n"
"  --merge mms-relay-os_6.10_bom.json \\\n"
"          mms-relay-app_2.0.0_bom.json \\\n"
"          mms-relay-bin_2.0.0_bom.json \\\n"
"  --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This writes `mms-relay-server_1.0.0_bom.json` with `metadata.component` set "
"to the server product, plus the notice and risk report over the merged "
"set. Each component keeps a `bomlens:layer` property, so you can still "
"filter by layer (`jq '.components[] | select(.properties[]?.value == "
"\"centos\")'`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The merge preserves each layer's `dependencies` graph (edges unioned by "
"ref), so the merged BOM keeps its transitive-dependency information and "
"passes the conformance check's transitive-dependency item. Cross-ecosystem "
"`bom-ref` collisions are rare; identical refs have their dependsOn lists "
"unioned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:109
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What makes a server SBOM incomplete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Hand-written SBOMs.** A `tool: manual` SBOM almost always omits "
"components. Always generate with a tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**`pkg:generic` components.** Use the standard purl types (`pkg:rpm`, "
"`pkg:maven`, and so on) so vulnerability matching works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Raw-directory scans with no metadata.** Scanning a folder of unpacked "
"install files, with no package database, leaves purls empty and the whole "
"result useless. Target a real rootfs or image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Scanning before the build.** Building the SBOM from a pre-build source "
"tree drops transitive dependencies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:116
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using the web UI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The OS and application layers can also run from the web UI (`$SBOM "
"--ui`). Put the rootfs under the folder where you launch the UI and use the "
"**Directory path** input, or scan a container image with the **Docker "
"image** input. Paths outside the launch folder are rejected for safety; to "
"scan a rootfs stored elsewhere, launch the UI with `--ui --mount <dir>` and "
"the folder appears as a read-only location in the Directory path "
"input. `--mount /` exposes the running host OS itself the same way (pseudo "
"filesystems such as `/proc` and `/sys` are skipped automatically, and "
"results still save under the launch folder). The static-link layer and the "
"optional merge are most direct from the CLI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/server-delivery.md:122
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Related**: [Input scenarios](by-input.md) | [Firmware "
"analysis](firmware.md) | [Validating a received SBOM](supplier-sbom.md) | "
"[CLI reference](../reference/cli.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Validate that an SBOM (CycloneDX/SPDX) you received meets your quality "
"criteria with BomLens, then analyze licenses and vulnerabilities into a risk "
"report."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Supplier SBOM validation guide"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"How to validate that an SBOM (JSON) received from a supplier or another team "
"meets your quality criteria. After validation, BomLens analyzes the licenses "
"and vulnerabilities and produces a risk report. You only need the SBOM file "
"— no source code required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:10
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When to use it"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use it when a supplier or another team hands you an SBOM file instead of "
"source, and you need to confirm the SBOM meets your quality criteria and "
"then check its licenses and vulnerabilities. The input can be CycloneDX or "
"SPDX (JSON, Tag-Value); it is converted to CycloneDX internally for "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The criteria check whether an SBOM is good enough for dependency "
"review. Requirements vary by organization; as one reference, see SK "
"Telecom's [supply chain security "
"guide](https://sktelecom.github.io/guide/supply-chain/for-suppliers/) and "
"its [SBOM "
"requirements](https://sktelecom.github.io/guide/supply-chain/for-suppliers/requirements/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Category | Criteria |\n"
"|----------|----------|\n"
"| Format | CycloneDX v1.3–1.6 or SPDX v2.2–2.3 |\n"
"| Required metadata | timestamp, tool info, top-level component name and "
"version |\n"
"| Required component fields | name, version, PURL in standard "
"`pkg:type/name@version` form (`pkg:generic` not allowed) |\n"
"| Completeness | both direct and transitive dependencies included |\n"
"| Recommended | supplier, license (SPDX ID), hash |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The accepted format ranges above are the SK Telecom submission "
"defaults. If your organization accepts a different range, override them with "
"the `CYCLONEDX_SPEC_VERSIONS`, `AI_CYCLONEDX_SPEC_VERSIONS` (AI SBOMs), and "
"`SPDX_SPEC_VERSIONS` environment variables (space-separated lists). They are "
"listed in the [Docker image environment "
"variables](../reference/docker-image.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Running it all at once"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Open the web UI, choose **SBOM upload**, and upload the file you received; "
"enter a project name and version, then run. A Yocto SPDX 2.2 build hands "
"over an `<image>.spdx.tar.zst` rather than a document — that archive uploads "
"here too, since it is the only SBOM such a build produces.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the SBOM leans Java (Maven), turn on **Deep CVE matching (NVD CPE)** in "
"the scan options. It checks older Maven libraries against NVD-only "
"vulnerabilities that other advisory sources miss, at the cost of a longer "
"scan. The option is offered on every base-image scan mode, not just SBOM "
"upload — it is hidden only for firmware and AI-model scans, which have no "
"package SBOM to extend. The first run downloads the deep-cve image once. It "
"is the same matching as the CLI's `--deep-cve`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui     # opens http://localhost:8080\n"
"#   Windows: double-click scripts\\sbom-ui.bat\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Installation is in [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Prefer no command line? See the [no-CLI quick start](../start/no-cli.md) "
"first. What follows is the CLI path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Pull the scanner image once (`docker pull "
"ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest`), then pass the SBOM file to `--analyze`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project supplier-app --version 2.0.0 \\\n"
"  --analyze \"./supplier-sbom.json\" \\\n"
"  --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`--analyze` turns on notice and security analysis automatically, so you do "
"not need to add `--all`. `--generate-only` leaves only the outputs in a "
"`{Project}_{Version}/` subfolder under the current directory and cleans up "
"the temporary working copy. For the remaining options, see the [usage "
"guide](../reference/cli.md#options-reference)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The four outputs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Output | File | Meaning |\n"
"|--------|------|---------|\n"
"| Conformance report | `{Project}_{Version}_conformance.{json,md,html}` | "
"whether the quality criteria are met, and what is missing |\n"
"| SBOM (converted) | `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json` | SPDX inputs converted "
"to CycloneDX 1.6; CycloneDX inputs keep their original spec version |\n"
"| Open-source notice | `{Project}_{Version}_NOTICE.{txt,html}` | components "
"grouped by license |\n"
"| Risk report | `{Project}_{Version}_risk-report.{md,html}` | conformance, "
"vulnerabilities, and licenses combined, with response deadlines |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Unlike a self-generated SBOM, a received SBOM additionally produces a "
"conformance report, and its summary goes into section 1 of the risk report."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The conformance report is the per-item check of whether the received SBOM "
"meets the quality criteria. Validation is based on the original input before "
"conversion, so even for SPDX it checks the fields of the original SPDX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If any required item falls short, it is a `fail`. The required items match "
"the criteria table in [When to use it](#when-to-use-it) — spec version range "
"(CycloneDX v1.3–1.6, SPDX v2.2–2.3), timestamp, tool info, top-level "
"component, name/version coverage, PURL coverage and syntax (standard "
"`pkg:type/name@version` form, no `pkg:generic`), and transitive "
"dependencies. AI SBOMs are also accepted at CycloneDX 1.7, which the AIBOM "
"toolchain emits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If a recommended item falls short, it is a `warn`, not a `fail`. Besides "
"license and hash coverage, this includes the advisory per-component fields "
"the regulatory baselines call for — SHA-512 checksum coverage, component "
"creator, component filename, source/distribution URI, the delivered-file "
"properties (marked review when no scan can see the artifact), and the file "
"component identifier coverage described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Name/version and PURL coverage are measured over package components only. A "
"binary or firmware SBOM also lists the delivered files as file components, "
"and a file on disk has no package version and no PURL type to carry, so "
"counting them would mark an SBOM short on a field that cannot exist "
"there. Files are still expected to be identified, by the identifier they do "
"carry: the file identifier check measures how many of them have a hash. An "
"SBOM that lists files and no packages at all is a `fail`, because "
"vulnerability matching keys on package identifiers and a file listing "
"answers none of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"One of the 2026 minimum elements asks the SBOM to say why a field is empty "
"when it is empty — whether the author could not establish the value or is "
"withholding it. An SBOM BomLens generated carries that statement for the "
"whole document, since a scan only ever produces the first case. A received "
"SBOM that says nothing about its absences is reported as a gap on that "
"element."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The cards at the top of the HTML report show pass/fail and the list of "
"missing items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Each check that corresponds to a regulatory baseline carries the reference "
"under its row, and a crosswalk section rolls the coverage up per framework — "
"BSI TR-03183-2 (the German technical guideline for the EU Cyber Resilience "
"Act) and the US SBOM minimum elements (2026). The crosswalk is reference "
"material and makes no compliance determination; the [AI model SBOM "
"guide](ai-model.md#regulatory-crosswalk) describes how it works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When a `fail` appears, tell whoever sent the SBOM which fields are missing "
"and ask them to fix it. The most common unmet items are a missing PURL, use "
"of `pkg:generic`, and missing transitive dependencies (only direct "
"dependencies included)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reading the risk report"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The risk report (`_risk-report`) is a document built by re-aggregating the "
"outputs above without a new scan. It has four parts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Requirements met — the conformance results table. If `fail`, the unmet items "
"are stated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Vulnerability tally and response deadlines — a severity tally plus the "
"recommended deadlines (a response plan or risk justification within 7 days "
"for Critical and 30 days for High), laid out in a table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "License summary — the notice and license coverage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "Next steps — guidance on a response plan."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SPDX input"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:91
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you supply SPDX (JSON, Tag-Value), it is converted to CycloneDX "
"internally with `syft convert` and then analyzed through the same "
"pipeline. Conformance validation is based on the original SPDX before "
"conversion, because metadata such as timestamp, tools, or transitive "
"dependencies can be normalized away during conversion. Some SPDX license "
"expressions may be simplified when moved to CycloneDX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:92
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Yocto images"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A Yocto build can produce its own SPDX SBOM, and BomLens reads it with a "
"dedicated parser rather than the generic SPDX path, because a Yocto document "
"carries two things the generic path loses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:97
#, markdown-text
msgid "To produce one, add the following to `local.conf` and build as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"INHERIT += \"create-spdx-3.0\"\n"
"INHERIT += \"vex\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:104
#, markdown-text
msgid "Which SPDX version a release can write is not a choice everywhere:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:110
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Release | SPDX by default | `create-spdx-3.0` available |\n"
"|---------|-----------------|-----------------------------|\n"
"| 4.0 Kirkstone (LTS) | 2.2 | **no** — the class does not exist in this "
"release |\n"
"| 5.0 Scarthgap (LTS) | 2.2 | yes |\n"
"| 5.1 Styhead and later | 3.0 | yes (it is the default) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"On Kirkstone the setting above cannot be used; that build writes SPDX 2.2, "
"which is read as described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Then point the scan at the build directory. You do not need to know where "
"the build put the SBOM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project my-image --version 1.0.0 \\\n"
"  --target ~/poky/build --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:121
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The build directory is recognized as one, and the image SBOM it published — "
"`tmp/deploy/images/<machine>/<image>.rootfs.spdx.json`, or `tmp-glibc/…` on "
"an OpenEmbedded build — is analyzed. The build tree itself is not walked: "
"scanning it as a directory would report sysroots and native build tools that "
"never ship in the image.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:123
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When several machines or images were built, the most recently written SBOM "
"is analyzed and all the candidates are listed in the log; pass a specific "
"one with `--analyze <file>` to choose another. A build that writes its "
"images somewhere else entirely (a relocated `DEPLOY_DIR`) is not found this "
"way either, so name that document the same way. When all you were sent is "
"the SBOM file, upload it in the web UI or pass it to `--analyze`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:125
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The web UI reads the same folder: pick it with the Directory input (mount it "
"first with `--ui --mount ~/poky/build`, or use Add folder in the desktop "
"app) and the detection runs exactly as it does on the command line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:126
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A build that produced no SPDX at all"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:129
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Turning `create-spdx` on is a build-configuration change, and whoever holds "
"a finished build directory cannot always make one. A build records what it "
"shipped regardless, and those records are read instead:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| What | Where | Gives |\n"
"|------|-------|-------|\n"
"| Image package manifest | `tmp/deploy/images/<machine>/<image>.manifest` | "
"the installed packages and their versions |\n"
"| License manifest | `tmp/deploy/licenses/**/license.manifest` | each "
"package's license and the recipe it came from |\n"
"| cve-check report | `tmp/log/cve/cve-summary.json` | per CVE, whether a "
"recipe patched it, judged it not applicable, or left it open |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:137
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is the weakest of the three inputs, and worth knowing why: there are no "
"CPEs, so vulnerability matching has only names and versions to work with, "
"and the CVE verdicts are only as complete as the build's own `cve-check` run "
"(a build that never ran it reports no verdicts rather than none "
"existing). No conformance report is produced either — conformance measures a "
"document someone sent you against submission criteria, and there is no "
"document here. Adding the two `local.conf` lines above and rebuilding "
"remains the better answer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:139
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the directory is a Yocto build but holds neither an SPDX document nor an "
"image manifest, the scan stops and names the two settings above rather than "
"falling back to a directory scan whose result would misrepresent the image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:141
#, markdown-text
msgid "What you get differs from a normal SBOM scan in two ways."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:143
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The component list contains only the packages installed in the image. A "
"Yocto document also describes every source archive the build consumed, which "
"is useful for provenance but would misrepresent what the product "
"ships. Those are left out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:145
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Vulnerabilities come from the build itself. Yocto runs a CVE analysis while "
"building and records a verdict per CVE, so it knows whether a recipe applied "
"the patch. Those verdicts are shown split three ways: patched during the "
"build, judged not applicable, and still open. Only the open ones are counted "
"as findings. On the reference `core-image-minimal` image this is the "
"difference between reporting 12255 vulnerabilities and reporting none, since "
"every one of them was already closed by the build."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:147
#, markdown-text
msgid "Two limits are worth knowing before you start."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SPDX 2.2 is read, but with less in it. Yocto 4.0 (Kirkstone) and 5.0 "
"(Scarthgap) emit SPDX 2.2 by default, and that form is not a document at "
"all: the deploy directory holds one `<image>.spdx.tar.zst` and nothing "
"else. Inside it are the image document, a document per installed package and "
"one per recipe. BomLens reads the archive itself — measured against the "
"published Yocto 5.0.14 `core-image-minimal`, it yields the same 36 packages "
"the image manifest lists, with their licenses and CPEs. What they do not "
"give is the build's CVE verdicts — only SPDX 3.0 records which CVEs a recipe "
"patched — so vulnerabilities are matched from the CPEs like any other SBOM, "
"and a CVE the build already patched can appear as open. Pull the image "
"document out of the archive and upload it alone and you get an almost empty "
"result, which is said rather than left to look like a clean scan. When a "
"build directory holds both formats, the SPDX 3.0 document is the one "
"analyzed even if the 2.2 one is newer. No conformance report is produced for "
"an archive: it is a bundle of documents rather than a submitted one, so "
"there is nothing to measure against the submission criteria.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Conformance checks that depend on PURL will fail. Yocto identifies packages "
"with CPE rather than PURL, so PURL coverage and the checks derived from it "
"cannot pass. The report says how many components carry a CPE instead, and "
"the row cites the baselines — BSI TR-03183-2 and the US SBOM minimum "
"elements — that accept either identifier. The verdict is the submission "
"criteria's, not theirs: PURL is required here because the default "
"vulnerability matching keys on it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:153
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Two more required checks behave differently on a Yocto image, for reasons in "
"the document rather than in the tool. The top-level component fails for want "
"of a version: bitbake writes the image package with a name and no "
"`software_packageVersion` (measured on the reference `core-image-minimal`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:155
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Uploads are capped at 100 MB. For scale, the reference `core-image-minimal` "
"document is 15.8 MB with 35 installed packages. A build directory scanned "
"with `--target` reads the file from disk, so the cap does not apply there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:156
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Asking for remediation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:159
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After validation and analysis, send the risk report (`_risk-report.html`) to "
"whoever sent the SBOM and ask for the following."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:162
#, markdown-text
msgid "Fix the conformance `fail` items and send the SBOM again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:162
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Prepare a response plan or risk justification for Critical vulnerabilities "
"within 7 days and High within 30 days (recommended deadlines)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:164
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Response tracking, exception approval, and history management are out of "
"scope for this tool — they belong to a separate vulnerability and risk "
"management system. This tool covers validating, analyzing, and reporting on "
"a single SBOM locally."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:170
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Validation is based on the presence and coverage of required fields. It does "
"not guarantee semantic accuracy such as whether a PURL points to the exact "
"package or whether a version is real."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:170
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Whether transitive dependencies are included is inferred from the presence "
"of edges in the dependency graph; it is not proof that the graph is "
"complete."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:170
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The accuracy of vulnerability and license analysis depends directly on the "
"quality of the input SBOM, especially PURL and version accuracy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:173
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Related**: [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md) | [Scenarios "
"guide](../guides/by-input.md) | [Notice and security "
"guide](../guides/reports.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/guides/upload.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Upload a generated SBOM to a Dependency-Track server or to TRUSCA's native "
"ingest endpoint."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/guides/upload.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Upload to Dependency-Track / TRUSCA"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/upload.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide covers how the scanner uploads a generated SBOM and how to target "
"TRUSCA's native ingest endpoint."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/upload.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After a scan, the SBOM is uploaded by default (`--generate-only` saves "
"locally and skips the upload). Choose the destination with `UPLOAD_TARGET`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/upload.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`dependency-track` (default): a regular Dependency-Track "
"server. Authenticates with `API_URL` and `API_KEY` (`X-Api-Key`) and "
"auto-creates the project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/upload.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`trusca`: TRUSCA's native ingest endpoint. It is not Dependency-Track "
"compatible, so the auth and inputs differ."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/upload.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "To upload to TRUSCA, prepare three things."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/upload.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "`API_URL`: the TRUSCA server URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/upload.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`API_KEY`: a Bearer token issued by TRUSCA (starts with `tos_`, developer "
"role)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/upload.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"project_id: the target TRUSCA project id (UUID). It must already exist; "
"there is no auto-create."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/upload.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"API_URL=\"https://<TRUSCA host>\" API_KEY=\"tos_...\" \\\n"
"  ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh \\\n"
"  --project \"MyApp\" --version \"1.2.3\" --all \\\n"
"  --trusca \"<project_id>\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/upload.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--trusca <id>` is shorthand for `--upload-target trusca` plus "
"`TRUSCA_PROJECT_ID`. Adjust the ref and release labels with `TRUSCA_REF` "
"(default `main`) and `TRUSCA_RELEASE` (default the `--version` value). On "
"acceptance it prints `202` and a scan id; track progress in the TRUSCA UI "
"(`GET /v1/scans/{id}`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/upload.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> TRUSCA ingest fills components, vulnerabilities, declared licenses, the "
"dependency graph, and the build gate. It cannot fill scancode-detected "
"licenses (`--deep-license`), the cosign signature (`--sign`), or source "
"preservation, since there is no source tree. Generate those locally with "
"`--generate-only` if you need them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/upload.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can upload without the CLI. On the New scan form, turn on the **Upload** "
"step, choose Dependency-Track or TRUSCA, and enter the server URL and access "
"token (plus the project id for TRUSCA). The scan runs and then uploads in "
"one step, using the same endpoints and authentication described above. The "
"URL and token are used for that run only and are not saved. See the [Web UI "
"reference](../reference/ui.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/index.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"BomLens is a local-first SBOM generator and open-source risk assessor. From "
"source code, containers, binaries, firmware, or an SBOM you received, it "
"produces a CycloneDX SBOM, an open-source notice, and a security and license "
"risk report — CLI or web UI, no SaaS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Array Element: hide
#: docs/index.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "toc"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/index.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate SBOMs and assess open-source risk, all locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A local-first SBOM generator and open-source risk assessor for a single "
"project — no SaaS, no account. From source code, a container image, a "
"binary, firmware, an SBOM you received, or a HuggingFace AI model, it "
"produces an [SBOM](concepts/what-is-sbom.md) (CycloneDX 1.6), an open-source "
"notice, and a security risk report in one run. For an AI model it builds a "
"CycloneDX ML-BOM and checks it against the [G7 minimum elements for "
"AI](guides/ai-model.md), whose clusters overlap with the EU AI Act's Annex "
"IV."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[Get started](start/first-scan.md){ .md-button .md-button--primary } [Try "
"the demo](https://bomlens.ospo.tw/demo/){ .md-button } [Download for Windows "
"(.exe)](https://github.com/sktelecom/bomlens/releases/latest/download/BomLens-Setup.exe){ "
".md-button }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[![Latest "
"release](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/sktelecom/bomlens)](https://github.com/sktelecom/bomlens/releases/latest)  "
"The Windows installer needs a Docker engine already running; see the [no-CLI "
"quick start](start/no-cli.md) below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/index.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Want to see what a result looks like before installing anything? The [live "
"demo](https://bomlens.ospo.tw/demo/) is the real web UI holding one finished "
"scan of each kind: a Spring Boot project from source, a container image, a "
"device firmware image, an AI model as a CycloneDX ML-BOM, and a supplier "
"SBOM checked against the format requirements. Nothing to install, and "
"nothing is uploaded: it is a frozen copy of results produced by ordinary "
"local runs."
