#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The output files BomLens produces — file list, when each is generated, "
"naming rules, and the SBOM structure summary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Artifacts reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The generated SBOM is CycloneDX 1.6 JSON. An SPDX 2.3 JSON copy, converted "
"from the final CycloneDX BOM, is produced by `--spdx` during a CLI scan or "
"on demand from the results screen in the UI. Both paths run the same "
"conversion and give the same file. CycloneDX remains the primary format, and "
"CycloneDX-only data (vulnerabilities, `bomlens:*` properties) is not carried "
"over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The filename is `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json` "
"(e.g. `MyApp_1.0.0_bom.json`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Output files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| File | When generated | Description |\n"
"|------|----------------|-------------|\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json` | always | SBOM (CycloneDX 1.6) |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_bom.spdx.json` | `--spdx` / `--all`, or Export as "
"SPDX 2.3 in the UI | SBOM (SPDX 2.3, converted from the CycloneDX output) "
"|\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_NOTICE.txt` / `.html` | `--notice` / `--all` / risk "
"report default | open-source notice |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_security.json` / `.md` / `.html` | `--security` / "
"`--all` / risk report default | Trivy security report |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_risk-report.md` / `.html` | default (all modes) — "
"omit with `--no-report` | open-source risk report |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_conformance.json` / `.md` / `.html` | `--analyze` | "
"format conformance report, with a regulatory crosswalk roll-up for every "
"SBOM (EU CRA via BSI TR-03183-2, the US SBOM minimum elements of 2026 — "
"reference only, no compliance determination). For an AI SBOM it also carries "
"the G7 checks and, for each advisory element still missing, the CycloneDX "
"fragment that would satisfy it. See a [rendered "
"example](../samples/aether-7b-5attn_conformance.html) |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_ai-profile.json` / `.md` | AI SBOM (`--model`, or "
"`--analyze` on an SBOM with a model component) | AI compliance profile: G7 "
"rollup, the closable gaps with their reference links, license-flagged "
"components, regulatory crosswalk, and the model risk assessment "
"(`riskAssessment`: per-model ok/conditional/caution/review verdicts with "
"conditions, reasons and the usage scenario; guidance, not legal advice). The "
"same rollup opens the conformance HTML, so there is no separate HTML profile "
"|\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_scancode.json` | `--deep-license` | raw scancode "
"result |\n"
"| `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json.sig` | `--sign` | cosign signature (with "
"`--spdx`, a `_bom.spdx.json.sig` is produced too) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`{P}` = project name, `{V}` = version (special characters are normalized to "
"`_`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The conditions above are the CLI flags. In the web UI and the desktop app "
"the same choices are the generation options on the New scan screen — Notice "
"and Security report — and every file produced is listed in the Artifacts "
"section of the results, downloadable per format or as one ZIP. SPDX is not a "
"scan option there: the SBOM card in that section has an **Export as SPDX "
"2.3** button that converts the finished BOM whenever you need it, and the "
"converted file joins the artifact list and the ZIP. The UI has no signing, "
"so an SPDX exported that way is unsigned; use `--spdx --sign` in the CLI "
"when you need a signature. See [Web UI and desktop app](ui.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SBOM structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: docs/reference/artifacts.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bomFormat          \"CycloneDX\"\n"
"specVersion        \"1.6\"\n"
"metadata\n"
"  ├── timestamp    generation time (ISO 8601)\n"
"  └── component    project info (name, version, type)\n"
"components[]\n"
"  ├── type         \"library\" | \"framework\" | \"application\"\n"
"  ├── name         component name\n"
"  ├── version      version\n"
"  ├── purl         Package URL (unique identifier)\n"
"  └── licenses[]   license info (SPDX ID)\n"
msgstr ""

