#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Call the BomLens scanner Docker image directly with docker run, for CI "
"runners, Kubernetes jobs, and other environments where the script cannot "
"live."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use the Docker image directly"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For everyday use we recommend the [`scan-sbom.sh`](../reference/cli.md) "
"script, which handles language detection, image selection, and volume mounts "
"for you. This document explains how to call the image directly with `docker "
"run` in environments where the script cannot live (CI runners, Kubernetes "
"jobs, and so on)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Images and tags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Image | Purpose |\n"
"|--------|------|\n"
"| `ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens` | Scanning and post-processing (canonical "
"name) |\n"
"| `ghcr.io/sktelecom/sbom-generator`, `ghcr.io/sktelecom/sbom-scanner` | "
"Aliases of the same image (former names, same digest) |\n"
"| `ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-firmware` | Firmware analysis (includes GPL "
"tools, opt-in) (legacy alias: sbom-scanner-firmware) |\n"
"| `ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-deep-cve` | Bundles grype for deep CVE matching "
"(opt-in). Used by the CLI's `--deep-cve` and by the web UI's Deep CVE "
"matching toggle, both of which pull it automatically as a sibling container "
"when it is not already the running image |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`latest` and version tags are available, and both `linux/amd64` and "
"`linux/arm64` are supported. Images are signed with cosign before "
"publishing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker pull ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is in the image"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is a lightweight image (based on python 3.12 slim) without language "
"toolchains. For source scans, transitive dependency resolution is handled by "
"the script, which pulls per-language cdxgen images separately. See "
"[Architecture](../concepts/architecture.md) for the structure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool | Version | Role |\n"
"|------|------|------|\n"
"| syft | v1.51.0 | Scans images, binaries, and directories |\n"
"| Trivy | v0.74.0 | Vulnerability report |\n"
"| cosign | v2.6.5 | SBOM signing |\n"
"| jq | — | SBOM normalization and notice generation |\n"
"| ScanCode Toolkit | 32.5.0 | Precise license detection (included only in "
"opt-in builds) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tool versions are pinned with `ARG` in `docker/Dockerfile`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Running directly"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Select the analysis mode with the `MODE` environment variable. All examples "
"below leave their outputs in the current directory and do not upload "
"anything (`UPLOAD_ENABLED=false`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze a Docker image"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker run --rm \\\n"
"  -v \"$(pwd)\":/host-output \\\n"
"  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \\\n"
"  -e MODE=IMAGE \\\n"
"  -e TARGET_IMAGE=\"nginx:alpine\" \\\n"
"  -e UPLOAD_ENABLED=false \\\n"
"  -e HOST_OUTPUT_DIR=/host-output \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_NAME=\"Nginx\" \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_VERSION=\"alpine\" \\\n"
"  ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze a binary file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker run --rm \\\n"
"  -v \"$(pwd)\":/target \\\n"
"  -v \"$(pwd)\":/host-output \\\n"
"  -e MODE=BINARY \\\n"
"  -e TARGET_FILE=/target/firmware.bin \\\n"
"  -e UPLOAD_ENABLED=false \\\n"
"  -e HOST_OUTPUT_DIR=/host-output \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_NAME=\"Firmware\" \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_VERSION=\"1.0\" \\\n"
"  ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze a source directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker run --rm \\\n"
"  -v \"$(pwd)\":/src \\\n"
"  -v \"$(pwd)\":/host-output \\\n"
"  -e MODE=SOURCE \\\n"
"  -e UPLOAD_ENABLED=false \\\n"
"  -e HOST_OUTPUT_DIR=/host-output \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_NAME=\"MyApp\" \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_VERSION=\"1.0.0\" \\\n"
"  ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:89
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In direct runs, `SOURCE` mode has syft read the package manifests inside the "
"container, so it may only capture direct dependencies. If you need "
"transitive dependencies, use `scan-sbom.sh`, which routes to the "
"per-language cdxgen images."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:90
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Notice and reports in one run"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In direct runs, the notice and security reports are off by default. Turn on "
"the following variables to get the same outputs as the CLI's `--all`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker run --rm \\\n"
"  -v \"$(pwd)\":/host-output \\\n"
"  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \\\n"
"  -e MODE=IMAGE \\\n"
"  -e TARGET_IMAGE=\"nginx:alpine\" \\\n"
"  -e GENERATE_NOTICE=true \\\n"
"  -e GENERATE_SECURITY=true \\\n"
"  -e GENERATE_REPORT=true \\\n"
"  -e UPLOAD_ENABLED=false \\\n"
"  -e HOST_OUTPUT_DIR=/host-output \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_NAME=\"Nginx\" \\\n"
"  -e PROJECT_VERSION=\"alpine\" \\\n"
"  ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:111
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:147
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Variable | Required | Default | Description |\n"
"|-----------|------|--------|------|\n"
"| `MODE` | Yes | `POSTPROCESS` | Analysis mode: `SOURCE`, `IMAGE`, `BINARY`, "
"`ROOTFS`, `FIRMWARE`, `ANALYZE` |\n"
"| `PROJECT_NAME` | Yes | — | Project name |\n"
"| `PROJECT_VERSION` | Yes | — | Project version |\n"
"| `TARGET_IMAGE` | Per mode | — | Image name for `IMAGE` mode (requires the "
"docker.sock mount) |\n"
"| `TARGET_FILE` | Per mode | — | File path for `BINARY`/`FIRMWARE` mode "
"(path inside the container) |\n"
"| `TARGET_DIR` | Per mode | — | Directory path for `ROOTFS` mode |\n"
"| `UPLOAD_ENABLED` | — | `true` | If `false`, save locally without uploading "
"(same as CLI `--generate-only`) |\n"
"| `HOST_OUTPUT_DIR` | — | — | Mounted path to copy the outputs to |\n"
"| `GENERATE_NOTICE` | — | `false` | Generate the open-source notice (CLI "
"`--notice`) |\n"
"| `GENERATE_SECURITY` | — | `false` | Generate the Trivy security report "
"(CLI `--security`) |\n"
"| `GENERATE_REPORT` | — | `false` | Generate the open-source risk analysis "
"report (off in direct runs, unlike the CLI default) |\n"
"| `ENRICH_MAVEN_CPE` | — | `true` | Attach an NVD-matchable `cpe:2.3` to "
"maven components (derived from the groupId) so a CPE-aware engine can reach "
"their NVD-only CVEs; unmapped groups get no CPE (skipped for AI SBOMs) |\n"
"| `ENRICH_GITHUB_CPE` | — | `true` | Attach an NVD-matchable `cpe:2.3` to a "
"small, hand-verified set of `pkg:github/` components (source-repository-only "
"coordinates, typical for large C/C++ projects with no package-manager "
"ecosystem) so a CPE-aware engine can reach their NVD-only CVEs; anything not "
"in the curated list gets no CPE (skipped for AI SBOMs) |\n"
"| `ENRICH_INTERPRETER_CPE` | — | `true` | Attach an NVD-matchable `cpe:2.3` "
"to a small, hand-verified set of interpreter components (e.g. Python "
"packaged as a conda or NuGet artifact) so a CPE-aware engine can reach their "
"NVD-only CVEs; anything not in the curated list gets no CPE (skipped for AI "
"SBOMs) |\n"
"| `SECURITY_NVD_VERIFY` | — | `false` | With `--deep-cve`: verify each grype "
"`nvd:cpe` finding against the live NVD version range and drop out-of-range "
"false positives (needs `NVD_API_KEY` + network; adds minutes). Off by "
"default — findings are kept and flagged version-unverified |\n"
"| `NVD_API_KEY` | For `SECURITY_NVD_VERIFY` | — | NVD API key used by the "
"deep-cve version filter; passed to the container by name only (never "
"inlined) |\n"
"| `ENRICH_EOL` | — | `true` | Flag components past their upstream "
"end-of-life from a bundled offline snapshot (skipped for AI SBOMs) |\n"
"| `ENRICH_MALICIOUS` | — | `true` | Flag components that are known-malicious "
"packages (typosquats, hijacked accounts) from a bundled offline OSV "
"snapshot. A separate signal from vulnerabilities: the response is removal "
"and credential rotation, not an upgrade |\n"
"| `ENRICH_OS_CONTEXT` | — | `true` | Synthesize an `operating-system` "
"component from distro package PURLs (rpm, deb, and apk). Trivy selects the "
"distro vulnerability feed from that component, so without it the OS packages "
"in a supplier SBOM or rootfs scan would get no OS CVE matches at all. No-op "
"when the SBOM has no recognizable distro packages — including a distro Trivy "
"carries no feed for, such as OpenWRT (skipped for AI SBOMs) |\n"
"| `STALENESS_ENRICH` | — | `false` | Add deps.dev version currency (how many "
"releases behind latest); needs network access |\n"
"| `ENRICH_HF_SECURITY` | — | `true` | AIBOM mode: read HuggingFace's "
"per-file security scan results (ClamAV + picklescan) into the ML-BOM; "
"metadata only, no file download |\n"
"| `API_KEY`, `API_URL` | For uploads | — | Upload credential and server "
"URL. DT uses `X-Api-Key`; TRUSCA uses a Bearer token |\n"
"| `UPLOAD_TARGET` | — | `dependency-track` | Upload destination: "
"`dependency-track` (DT-compatible) or `trusca` (native ingest, not "
"DT-compatible) |\n"
"| `TRUSCA_PROJECT_ID` | When `trusca` | — | Target TRUSCA project id "
"(UUID). Must already exist (no auto-create) |\n"
"| `TRUSCA_REF` | — | `main` | Ingest ref label |\n"
"| `TRUSCA_RELEASE` | — | `PROJECT_VERSION` | Ingest release label |\n"
"| `BOMLENS_MAVEN_FULL_GRAPH` | — | — | Maven source scans: set `1` to keep "
"the full resolved graph instead of filtering to compile/runtime scope |\n"
"| `BOMLENS_NODE_FULL_GRAPH` | — | — | Node.js source scans: set `1` to keep "
"the full dev-plus-production graph instead of the production-only set |\n"
"| `BOMLENS_KEEP_BUILD_OUTPUT` | — | — | Source scans: set `1` to leave the "
"resolved tree in place. By default the scan restores the files its resolvers "
"rewrote (`go.mod`, `go.sum`, `Cargo.lock`, `Gemfile.lock`, "
"`Package.resolved`) and removes the build directories they created, so the "
"scanned project is handed back as it was |\n"
"| `CYCLONEDX_SPEC_VERSIONS` | — | `1.3 1.4 1.5 1.6` | Accepted CycloneDX "
"spec versions for the conformance check (space-separated); overrides the "
"default range |\n"
"| `AI_CYCLONEDX_SPEC_VERSIONS` | — | `1.3 1.4 1.5 1.6 1.7` | Accepted "
"CycloneDX versions for AI SBOMs (ML-BOM), which additionally allow 1.7 |\n"
"| `SPDX_SPEC_VERSIONS` | — | `SPDX-2.2 SPDX-2.3` | Accepted SPDX spec "
"versions for the conformance check |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/reference/docker-image.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> TRUSCA's (formerly TrustedOSS Portal) native ingest endpoint (`POST "
"/v1/projects/{id}/sbom-ingest`, Bearer auth) is not Dependency-Track "
"compatible. To push to a regular Dependency-Track server, keep "
"`UPLOAD_TARGET=dependency-track` (the default).\n"
msgstr ""

